-- 026_seed_photo_albums.sql
-- One-time backfill so the Admin → Photo Albums page and the public Photo
-- Gallery share the same database records.
--
-- The public gallery (/media/photos) reads published albums from the albums
-- table via getPublishedAlbums() and only falls back to the static catalog
-- (lib/photoAlbums.ts) when the table is empty. The albums table was empty on
-- the hosted project, so the admin (which is DB-only) showed nothing while the
-- public gallery rendered the static fallback. This migration seeds those same
-- albums (plus their photo media references and album_photos links) from the
-- canonical catalog, preserving slugs, titles, descriptions, photo order, and
-- cover photos exactly as rendered today.
--
-- Idempotent: every insert uses deterministic UUIDs with on conflict (id) do
-- nothing, so re-running is a no-op and never creates duplicates.

-- 1. Media rows for gallery photos (type photo, published, static public URLs).
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- 2. Albums (published so the public gallery renders them, matching today's output).
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- 3. Album photo links (preserving photo order).
on conflict (id) do nothing;
